#comment E is the 4-vertex closed curve below. Down z (the xy view) its first
#comment and third edges cross at (1,1), separated in z, so project(E) is the
#comment single-crossing diagram carried here -- verified with
#comment `knoodlesimplify -s=0`, which is exactly the embedding->PD converter.
#comment Rotating by x->y->z->x carries the crossing out of the xy view, so
#comment project(R*E) is a crossingless circle: the next record carries no
#comment diagram, which is what a 0-crossing summand looks like in a trace.
#comment
#comment A rotation is an isotopy, so the link type is the same on both sides
#comment (an unknot either way) while the DIAGRAM changes -- which is the whole
#comment point of the kind. Generated and checked 2026-09-20.
